# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LYFE — environment
#
# Every var below is optional. With none of them set the app runs
# entirely on mocks, which is what makes `npm run dev` work for a
# designer with no credentials. `GET /api/health` reports which
# adapters are actually live — check it after every deploy, because a
# misconfigured backend degrades to mock data silently.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Which product this instance is ──
# 1 = the Dashboard basique of sprint Prio 02, seven screens. 2 = every
# screen this repository renders. Defaults to 1, and /api/health reports
# the lot in force — a deploy that means to show the contracted
# dashboard and reads 2 is showing screens nobody bought.
LYFE_LOT=1

# ── Data backend ──
# Both required together. Set neither to stay on mock data. They point at
# the Business Service's root; docs/LOT1_API_CONTRACT.md is what it has
# to answer, and `node tools/mock-api.mjs` is a double that does:
#
#   node tools/mock-api.mjs &
#   LYFE_LOT=1 LYFE_DATA=http \
#     LYFE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3311 LYFE_API_TOKEN=mock npm start
LYFE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.lyfe.ma/v1
LYFE_API_TOKEN=

# Forces one of the three data drivers — http · db · static — over the
# rule in src/lib/data/mode.ts. Worth setting in UAT so a stray
# .data/lyfe.db cannot quietly take over if one of the two vars above is
# missing. /api/health reports which driver is live, and why.
LYFE_DATA=

# ── Who can sign in ──
#
# The portal's credential store is `partner_accounts`, and `db/seed.mjs`
# writes seven fixture accounts into it so a clone and the demo are
# walkable. `GET /api/health` reports `demoAccounts` and the data driver,
# which together say whether anybody can get in.
#
# The password those rows are written with. Defaults to `demo`, which is
# what the documented walkthrough uses. A deployment that outlives the
# demo sets this — or deletes the rows.
LYFE_SEED_PASSWORD=
#
# Re-enables the seven pairs that are still written as literals in
# src/lib/auth/accounts.ts. Without a database they are the only door and
# are always live; with one, they are consulted only when this is exactly
# `1`. Audit item E-01 is why: seven accounts sharing one in-source
# password, one of them the account that validates listings. Set it to
# get a demo signing in against a database whose account rows are
# missing; do not set it on a deployment serving real partners.
LYFE_DEMO_ACCOUNTS=
#
# Stops `db/bootstrap.mjs` writing the fixture accounts into a database
# that has venues and no accounts at all. That combination means nobody
# can sign in, so the bootstrap fills it; one existing account is enough
# for it to leave the table alone. Set this only for a deployment that
# means to have venues and no way in.
LYFE_SKIP_DEMO_ACCOUNTS=
#
# Skips db/bootstrap.mjs entirely — no schema, no seed. For the afternoon
# the database is unreachable and a front-end fix has to ship anyway.
LYFE_SKIP_DB_BOOTSTRAP=

# ── AI (Anthropic) ──
# The SDK also accepts ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN or an `ant auth login`
# profile; with either of those, set LYFE_AI_ENABLED=true so the app
# knows to use the real advisor.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# true  — force the Claude advisor (use with non-API-key credentials)
# false — kill switch: fall back to the mock advisor without a redeploy
LYFE_AI_ENABLED=

# ── App connections ──
# HMAC secret for POST /api/webhooks/lyfe. Without it the endpoint
# returns 503 rather than accepting unverified writes.
LYFE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
